---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { products } from '../data/products.mjs';
import { repositories } from '../data/repositories.mjs';
import { distributionMatrix, publicDownloadUrl, publicOciImage } from '../data/distributions.mjs';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const artifacts = distributionMatrix.desktop.map(a => ({ ...a, url: publicDownloadUrl(a) })).filter(a => a.url);
const images = distributionMatrix.oci.images.map(i => ({ ...i, published: publicOciImage(i) })).filter(i => i.published);
const channels = [
  ['Linux', 'x86-64', 'Public desktop downloads', 'Self-contained AppImages for vibe-view and vibe-sketch, available on this page.'],
  ['macOS', 'Apple Silicon', 'Paid Mac App Store', 'Complete application packages with their required runtimes. Current local desktop previews do not establish Store availability.'],
  ['Windows', 'x86-64', 'Paid Microsoft Store', 'Native application packages with their required runtimes. Platform qualification and Store publication remain separate steps.'],
];
---
<Base title="Downloads and installation — vibe-qc" description="Current source installation routes, desktop implementation status and platform distribution channels for the vibe scientific toolset. MPL-2.0 applications and Apache-2.0 QVF.">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content" class="wrap downloads">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">official distribution matrix</span>
      <h1>Choose a tool.<br />Check its availability.</h1>
      <p>Download self-contained Linux desktops for vibe-view and vibe-sketch. macOS and Windows editions are planned paid purchases through their respective app stores.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="published-packages">
      <span class="eyebrow">verified package links</span>
      <h2 id="published-packages">Linux desktop downloads.</h2>
      <p>Free public downloads for x86-64 Linux. Python and application dependencies are included. These initial Linux builds were tested on Debian 12; a standard graphical desktop is required.</p>
      {artifacts.length === 0 && images.length === 0 ? <p>No qualified binary package or suite image is listed here. Use the project installation guides above; do not infer a package URL from its version or filename.</p> : <div class="grid">
        {artifacts.map(artifact => <article class="card"><h3>{artifact.product} · {artifact.platform}</h3><p>{artifact.architecture} · {artifact.sizeLabel}</p><p>{artifact.qualification}</p><p><a class="download-button" href={artifact.url}>Download {artifact.product} for Linux ↓</a></p><div class="route-links"><a href={artifact.checksumsUrl}>SHA-256 checksums ↗</a><a href={artifact.sourceUrl}>Corresponding source ↗</a></div><details><summary>Package SHA-256</summary><code>{artifact.sha256}</code></details></article>)}
        {images.map(image => <article class="card"><h3>{image.label}</h3><p>{image.ociPlatform}</p><code>{image.published.pinnedReference}</code></article>)}
      </div>}
      <p>After downloading, verify the SHA-256 checksum, make the AppImage executable and launch it as a regular user. Without FUSE, run the AppImage with <code>--appimage-extract</code>, then launch <code>squashfs-root/AppRun</code>. Linux updates currently use replacement downloads; these packages do not activate an updater feed.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="install-now">
      <span class="eyebrow">available installation routes</span>
      <h2 id="install-now">Start with the installation guide.</h2>
      <div class="grid install-grid">
        {products.map(product => <article class="card">
          <h3>{product.name}</h3>
          <p>{product.repository ? 'Public source snapshots. Follow the guide for dependencies and a dedicated environment; choose a published source tag when pinning a version.' : 'Browser and desktop workflows. The Linux AppImage and its corresponding source are public downloads on this page.'}</p>
          <p class="product-license"><a href={product.licenseGuide}>{product.license} license &amp; notices ↗</a></p>
          <div class="route-links">
            <a href={product.installGuide}>Installation guide ↗</a>
            <a href={`${base}products/${product.id}/`}>Product details ↗</a>
            {product.repository ? <><a href={product.repository}>Source repository ↗</a><a href={`${product.repository}/tags`}>Source tags ↗</a><a href={`${product.repository}/releases`}>Published releases ↗</a></> : <a href="#published-packages">Linux desktop &amp; corresponding source ↗</a>}
          </div>
        </article>)}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="desktop-status">
      <span class="eyebrow">implemented desktop workflows</span>
      <h2 id="desktop-status">Browser and desktop, with version-specific runtimes.</h2>
      <div class="grid install-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>vibe-view</h3><p>Browser, Electron desktop, terminal and headless interfaces are implemented. Current Apple Silicon package tooling bundles Python, PyVista, VTK, Trame and RDKit for macOS 14 or newer. The Linux AppImage also bundles its interpreter and viewer libraries; Windows packaging is being prepared for the Microsoft Store.</p><a href="/vibe-view/docs/desktop.html">Viewer desktop guide ↗</a></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>vibe-sketch</h3><p>Browser and Electron desktop workflows include Open, Save, recent files, import and export. The Linux AppImage bundles Python, RDKit, QVF and the editor. Apple Silicon tooling also bundles the runtime for macOS 14 or newer.</p><a href="/vibe-sketch/docs/desktop.html">Sketcher desktop guide ↗</a></article>
      </div>
      <p class="availability-note">Local ad-hoc-signed builds do not establish trusted signing, notarization or Store acceptance. The former vibe-view 2.9.0 candidates are historical records, not current download options.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="binary-channels">
      <span class="eyebrow">platform distribution channels</span>
      <h2 id="binary-channels">Linux downloads now. Store editions to follow.</h2>
      <p>Linux desktop packages for the viewer and sketcher are available here. Mac App Store and Microsoft Store editions will be available for purchase after Store publication; purchase links are not yet available.</p>
      <div class="channel-table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Platform</th><th scope="col">Initial architecture</th><th scope="col">Channel</th><th scope="col">Package scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>{channels.map(row => <tr>{row.map((cell,i) => i === 0 ? <th scope="row">{cell}</th> : <td>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p>Linux desktop downloads for vibe-view and vibe-sketch are public and do not require supporter membership. macOS and Windows versions will be available for purchase through the Mac App Store and Microsoft Store respectively; Store listings are not yet available. Building published source does not require a purchase or membership; corresponding source and notices remain accessible.</p>
      <p>vibe-sketch uses MPL-2.0 too; its Linux download includes a link to the matching source archive. Bundled third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="format-and-source">
      <span class="eyebrow">independent source projects</span>
      <h2 id="format-and-source">QVF and the source directory.</h2>
      <p>QVF remains Apache-2.0. Its specification, schemas and reference toolkit are independently versioned; the applications use MPL-2.0. A QVF archive retains the licensing and provenance of its own contents.</p>
      <div class="source-list">{repositories.map(repository => <article><h3>{repository.name}</h3><p>{repository.role}</p><a href={repository.github || `${base}products/vibe-sketch/#install`}>{repository.github ? 'Source repository ↗' : 'Access & setup ↗'}</a></article>)}</div>
      <p class="reviewed">Feature and availability review: {distributionMatrix.lastReviewed}. Check the installation guide for the version you intend to run.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<style>
  .download-button { display: inline-block; padding: 12px 18px; background: var(--phase-pos); color: #10201b; border-radius: 5px; font-weight: 600; }
  details { margin-top: 18px; font-size: 12px; }
  .downloads { padding-bottom: 80px; }
  .download-section { padding: 40px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(25px, 3vw, 36px); line-height: 1.2; margin: 14px 0 24px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 22px; }
  p { color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.65; }
  .install-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-block: 28px; }
  .route-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 20px; font-size: 14px; }
  a { color: var(--phase-pos); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .product-license { font-size: 13px; }
  .availability-note { padding: 18px 22px; background: var(--surface-2); border-left: 2px solid var(--phase-pos); }
  .channel-table { overflow-x: auto; margin-block: 28px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; }
  th, td { padding: 15px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; font-size: 14px; }
  thead { background: var(--surface-2); }
  td { color: var(--slate); }
  .source-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 28px; margin: 30px 0; }
  .reviewed { font-size: 13px; }
  code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media(max-width:650px) { .install-grid, .source-list { grid-template-columns:1fr; } th, td { padding:12px; min-width:120px; } }
</style>
